\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your Role
\f1\b0 \
You have been hired as a consultant for UN Women, an international organization dedicated to advancing gender equality and empowering women. Your task is to assess whether the increase in the share of women in national parliaments has led to meaningful improvements in gender equality, as measured by the\'a0
\f0\b Gender Inequality Index (GII) in the 2010s
\f1\b0 .\
\'a0\

\f0\b The Context
\f1\b0 \
Over the past few decades, many countries have implemented policies\'97such as gender quotas and other electoral reforms\'97to increase women\'92s representation in politics. Advocates argue that greater female participation in legislatures leads to stronger commitments to gender-equitable policies, including investments in women\'92s health, education, and economic participation. However, we need rigorous empirical evidence to determine whether this relationship holds across countries and to understand the magnitude of the impact.\
\'a0\

\f0\b Your Task
\f1\b0 \
Using a dataset covering multiple countries over a couple of decades, you will:\
\'95\'a0
\f0\b Clearly define the (causal) question and provide a motivation for it.
\f1\b0 \
\'95\'a0
\f0\b Specify and estimate an appropriate regression model:
\f1\b0 \'a0Identify key independent and dependent variables.\
\'95\'a0
\f0\b Perform diagnostic tests:
\f1\b0 \'a0Assess whether key econometric assumptions hold (e.g., heteroskedasticity, omitted variable bias, multicollinearity).\
\'95\'a0
\f0\b Interpret and communicate your findings:
\f1\b0 \'a0Present results clearly, explaining their statistical and policy significance.\
\'95\'a0
\f0\b Discuss policy implications:
\f1\b0 \'a0What do your findings suggest for governments, international organizations, and advocates working to reduce gender inequality?\
\'a0\

\f0\b Your Constraints
\f1\b0 \
1. You have 90 minutes to complete the analysis.\
2. You may use any available resources but must work independently.\
3. Your responses should be structured, concise, and supported by statistical evidence.\
\'a0\

\f0\b Your Deliverables
\f1\b0 \
1.
\f0\b Short Responses:
\f1\b0 \'a0A structured write-up answering each question concisely, with relevant regression tables and figures included as file uploads or screenshots where applicable.\'a0
\f0\b (Max 150 words per response.)
\f1\b0 \
2.
\f0\b R Script:
\f1\b0 \'a0A fully reproducible script that replicates all statistical analyses, to be uploaded at the end of the quiz where prompted.\
\'a0\

\f0\b The Dataset + Code
\f1\b0 \
You are given this dataset along with a codebook (in a separate sheet in the same file) for your analysis:\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://canvas.ucsd.edu/courses/71997/files/16882500?wrap=1"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 cross country dataset.xlsx}}\
